---
title: NMBL — write HTML the way you think
description: An indentation-based template syntax that compiles to your framework.
draft: false
tags:
  - intro
  - demo
---

// A standalone .nmbl file. Structure-first markup that compiles to
// Svelte / Vue / Astro / JSX — no closing tags, no <div> soup.
//! This rendered comment becomes an HTML comment in the output.

main#app.page.dark
  //─ Header: id + class shorthand, bound attrs, a component ───────
  header.hero(data-section="hero")
    img.hero__avatar(:src :alt width=48)
    h1.hero__title Welcome to {product.name}
    p.hero__tagline
      | {product.tagline}
      Badge(text=`v${product.version}` color="green" rounded)

  //─ Embedded markdown — built-in CommonMark + GFM ────────────────
  section.prose:md
    ## Why NMBL?

    Author **structure first**. No closing tags, just indentation. Prose
    like this lives in a `:md` block, so [links](/), `code`, and **bold**
    all just work — and `{ interpolation }` still flows through.

    - Compiles to your framework's native template
    - Markdown where you want it, markup where you need it

  //─ Control flow + the portable @each form ───────────────────────
  section.features
    h2 Features
    @if(features.length)
      ul.feature-list
        @each(feature, i of features :key="feature.id")
          li.feature
            span.feature__num {i + 1}
            a.feature__link(href={feature.url}) {feature.title}
            @if(feature.isNew)
              Badge(text="new" color="blue" outline)
            @elseif(feature.deprecated)
              Badge(text="old" color="red")
    @else
      p.empty Nothing to show yet.

  //─ A form: void elements, block expansion, commented attr ───────
  footer.signup
    form(action="/subscribe" method="post")
      label > input(type="email" name="email" placeholder="you@example.com" required)
      button(
        type="submit"
        // disabled            ← comment out a single attribute
        onClick={() => subscribe()}
      ) Get updates

  //─ Raw passthrough: an SVG icon is kept verbatim ────────────────
  div.icon
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20">
    <path d="M12 2 2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5Z" fill="currentColor"/>
    </svg>

script:
  // a glued `:` opens a raw content block — never parsed as NMBL
  const product = getProduct();
  if (1 < 2) console.log('plain JS, passed through untouched');

style:
  .page { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .hero__title { font-size: 2rem; }
  .feature__num { opacity: 0.5; }
